{"subnet":5,"name":"Hone","own_description":"Hone (SN5) is an RLVR subnet: reinforcement learning from verifiable rewards. Miners are paid to solve real software-engineering tasks- repository patches submitted as git diffs and terminal tasks submitted as scripts with full trajectories. Validators lease tasks from a problem server and grade every response deterministically in isolated Docker verifiers, so rewards reflect verified outcomes only. Each scored solution becomes high-quality, verifiable RL training data for post-training code and agent models. Docs: https://github.com/hone-subnet-org/hone-subnet \u00b7 Dashboard: https://honedashboard.com","site":"https://honedashboard.com","code":"https://github.com/hone-subnet-org/hone-subnet","days_of_history":30.0,"new_contest_took_over_this_number":false,"fee_now_usd":72.26,"fee_now_tao":0.3936,"fee_lowest_usd":32.87,"fee_highest_usd":235.43,"collateral_share":0.0,"slots_taken":256,"slots":256,"protected_hours":36.0,"new_entries":{"made_2_to_14_days_ago":360,"still_in":41,"fee_back_so_far":83,"typical_fee_paid_usd":51.08,"typical_pay_a_day_usd":26.96,"typical_pay_a_day_a_week_ago_usd":26.68,"days_for_todays_fee_at_that_pay":2.7},"followed_entries":{"made_14_to_30_days_ago":471,"entered_from":"2026-10-25","entered_to":"2026-11-10","wallets":79,"typical_fee_paid_usd":77.26,"earning_after_7_days":147,"in_but_under_1_usd_a_day_after_7_days":0,"earning_after_14_days":122,"in_but_under_1_usd_a_day_after_14_days":0,"paid_at_least_their_fee_by_now":219,"typical_result_usd":-8.86,"result_lower_quarter_usd":-36.95,"result_upper_quarter_usd":402.69,"ended_behind":242,"ended_about_even":17,"ended_ahead":212},"all_entries_in_window":{"entries":893,"wallets":144,"fees_paid_usd":64299.84,"paid_back_usd":146324.15,"still_in":200,"earning_today":190,"fees_of_entries_missed_between_readings_usd":0.0},"paid_today":{"usd_a_day_to_entrants":6563.7,"wallets_paid_5_usd_a_day_or_more":34,"largest_wallet_share":0.1389,"five_largest_wallets_share":0.5353},"pack":null,"mining_note":{"read_on":"2026-11-23","commit":"db5b106c5335bccc6924fb4174c0fdc9db27c16b","repository":"https://github.com/hone-subnet-org/hone-subnet","paragraphs":["A Hone miner solves a coding task with a Git patch or Bash script, then uploads it with a record of the model\u2019s work and signs the response. Validators, the participants who score the miners\u2019 work, need a public TCP port to reach the miner. The demo uses a funded, registered hotkey, the key a miner works with, and a Bedrock API key for paid model calls. It needs temporary disk space equal to the compressed task plus twice its expanded size, and no CPU, GPU memory or uptime minimum is stated.","Every hidden check must pass to earn one point, and speed adds no bonus. Validators pool up to 50 results per validator per miner over four days, and although the README describes an average, the code divides by at least 30 observations. Positive scores share rewards by rank, so each miner gets 99.5% of the weight above it, with ties favoring the lower UID.","The policy cites 36 hours of registration protection and schedules rounds 38 blocks apart. A lease needs ten minutes left at dispatch, but the demo allows at most 280 seconds by default, including 20 for uploads. The demo\u2019s example selects the test network, while subnet 5 runs on Finney. Once observed, an offline miner can receive zeros on completed rounds. Read from https://github.com/hone-subnet-org/hone-subnet at commit db5b106 on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 29 source checks, 28 held, 0 did not hold and 1 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run,